    "https://www.concordia.ca/hr/jobs.html": {
      "title": "Human Resources",
      "description": "Careers | Human Resources - Concordia University Skip to main content Info for Future students Current students Alumni & friends Faculty & staff Employers Parents Media Quick links Undergraduate Welcome Guide Graduate Welcome Guide Academic dates Student Hub Student Service Centre (Birks) International Students Office (ISO) All academic resources IT services Library Safety & prevention Exchanges & partnerships Printing Wi-Fi access Concordia app Apply Visit Give fr Human Resources Concordia Directories Search Search Close Careers Working at Concordia Current opportunities Employment equity Salary scales Pay equity Pension & benefits Pension & benefits overview Health plan Dental plan Pension plan Group RSP Life insurance plans Accident insurance plan Pensioners' Corner Employee Assistance Program Labour agreements Training & development About HR Meet HR Contact HR Policies & forms News & notices Glossary Apply Visit Give Useful links Maps Safety & prevention Wi-Fi access Printing IT support Library Contact us Concordia app Info for Future students Current students Alumni & friends Faculty & staff Employers Parents Media Quick links Undergraduate Welcome Guide Graduate Welcome Guide Academic dates Student Service Centre (Birks) International Students Office (ISO) Exchanges & partnerships All academic resources fr Open search form Concordia University Human Resources Careers Working at Concordia Current job opportunities Engage with big questions. Search for solutions and make positive contributions to society. Concordia creativity powers Montreal and connects us to the world. Work to redefine the 21st-century university. Concordia is a Montreal Top Employer The university’s workplace polices, family-friendly benefits, and pension & health plans received praise in the 2026 competition. Read the story Why work at Concordia? With more than 7,000 faculty and staff, Concordia enables individuals to grow, contribute and innovate, whatever their careers. The university offers: A highly diverse community in one of the most cosmopolitan cities in the world. A leading-edge teaching and research environment. Competitive compensation and benefits, opportunities to learn and develop — and more. Learn about Concordia Training & skills development Concordia provides faculty and staff with the tools and information they need to develop and grow their skills and competencies through in-house and online training programs. Development opportunities Health & dental Concordia's health and dental plans help faculty and staff pay for certain expenses. Health plan Dental plan Pension The Pension Plan for the Employees of Concordia University is a worry-free way to save for retirement. Pension plan Employee assistance The Employee Assistance Program is a confidential counselling, referral and information service. Employee Assistance Program Campus life Not only does Concordia have a unique, vibrant and rich campus life, the university also enjoys the benefit of having two campuses that are distinct and diverse. From state-of-the-art facilities for research and experimentation, to renovated office spaces and a leafy campus quad, there is a place for everyone. Discover more about life in Montreal Community involvement Public engagement and sustainability are deeply rooted in the Concordia identity. Faculty, staff and students are staying connected with the community and making a difference. There are many ways to stay informed and get involved at Concordia. Read about the Concordia Community Campaign Visit the Sustainability Hub News A round of a-paws for this year’s Shuffle pets August 27, 2026 Concordia honours more than 230 faculty and staff retirees at special event July 7, 2026 Theodore Stathopoulos appointed vice-provost, faculty development and inclusion June 23, 2026 More news Events SEP 16 Discover the people who make campus happen Wednesday, 10 a.m. – 3 p.m. SEP 24 Discover the people who make campus happen Thursday, 10 a.m. – 3 p.m. Calendar Concordia University on LinkedIn Back to top © Concordia University Human Resources Careers Pension & benefits Labour agreements Training & development About HR Contact us Concordia employee? Log in to Carrefour Contact us 514-848-2424, ext. 3666 Fax: 514-848-2844 hr-reception@concordia.ca Get in touch with HR Office hours Monday to Friday: 9 a.m. to 5 p.m. Visit us Room FB-1130 (11th floor) 1250 Guy St. Montreal, QC  H3H 2S7 Faubourg Building (FB) Mailing address Concordia University Attn. Human Resources 1455 De Maisonneuve Blvd. W. Montreal, QC  H3G 1M8 CANADA Territorial acknowledgement Concordia University is located on unceded Indigenous lands. The Kanien’kehá:ka Nation is recognized as the custodians of Tiohtià:ke/Montreal. Central 514-848-2424 | Emergency 514-848-3717 Safety & prevention | Accessibility | Privacy | Terms | Cookie settings | Contact us | Site feedback © Concordia University.  Montreal, QC, Canada"
